# Project: Ownership

Purpose:
  Define ownership rules for project elements.
  Every project element MUST have one clear owner.

Rules:
  [PO1] Every project element (domain, module, feature, component) MUST have one clear owner.
  [PO2] Ownership is declared at the element level, not inferred from filesystem paths.
  [PO3] A component's owner is the same as its parent module's owner unless explicitly overridden.
  [PO4] Code ownership implies review authority for that code.
  [PO5] Documentation ownership is separate from code ownership but should align.

Example:
  payments (module)
    owns: payment state, payment rules, payment database model

  refund (feature)
    owns: refund behavior, refund workflow

